<article class="env-remark" id="07YE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07YE">Remark <span data-tag="07YE">98.21.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{X}$ be a category fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. Let $A$ be an $S$-algebra. There is a notion of a <em>short exact sequence</em> </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (x, A_1' \to A) \to (x, A_2' \to A) \to (x, A_3' \to A)  \]
</div>
  <p> of deformation situations: we ask the corresponding maps between the kernels $I_ i = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(A_ i' \to A)$ give a short exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to I_3 \to I_2 \to I_1 \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> of $A$-modules. Note that in this case the map $A_3' \to A_1'$ factors through $A$, hence there is a canonical isomorphism $A_1' = A[I_1]$. </p>
</article>